---
layout: shell.webc
title: Components
description: The components and layouts in the Norn packages, rendered from the packages themselves.
---
<h1>Components</h1>
<p class="lead">
	Norn is a set of WebC components and layouts for Eleventy. This preview renders each one from its package, with its examples, props,
	slots, and custom properties.
</p>
<p webc:if="!$data.catalog.components.length">The packages hold no components yet, so there is nothing to show; each one appears here as it lands.</p>
<template webc:for="category of $data.catalog.categories.filter((entry) => entry.components.length)" webc:nokeep>
	<h2 @text="category.title"></h2>
	<p @text="category.description"></p>
	<ul role="list" class="cards">
		<li webc:for="component of category.components">
			<h3><a :href="component.url" @text="component.name"></a></h3>
			<p @text="component.summaryText"></p>
		</li>
	</ul>
</template>
<h2>Packages</h2>
<p>Each component ships in one of three packages.</p>
<ul>
	<li webc:for="pkg of $data.catalog.packages"><code @text="pkg.name"></code> <span @text="pkg.version"></span>: <span @text="pkg.description"></span></li>
</ul>
